{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Anecdotes and Personal Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Childhood Lessons", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Stressing <span class=\"italic\">You</span> and <span class=\"italic\">I</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You stress <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">you</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I</span></span> to add meaning and emphasis to a statement.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you stress a word, you make it longer, louder and a little higher tone. You can put stress on a word to emphasize it and make your meaning clearer. <br/>You stress <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">you</span></span> or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">I</span></span> when you want to emphasize something about a person that is not expected.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'm good. But how about <span class=\"strong\">you</span>?</span><ul><li>When you put stress on <span class=\"strong\">you</span>, you shift the emphasis to the other person.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read these sentences with stress on the bolded words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Well ... maybe <span class=\"strong\">I</span> was much more gullible than <span class=\"strong\">you</span> were.</li><li>I don't know about <span class=\"strong\">you</span>, but <span class=\"strong\">I</span> believed them all! </li><li><span class=\"strong\">I</span> always wear a sweater. Do <span class=\"strong\">you</span>?</li><li>As an adult, <span class=\"strong\">I</span> no longer believe in easy answers. What about <span class=\"strong\">you</span>? </span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Intonation of Finished and Unfinished Ideas", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Intonation tells us a lot about how someone feels and whether they have completed their thoughts or not. It is important to listen carefully to the rise and fall of people's voices. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In English, there there are three intonation patterns:<ol><li>Falling</li><li>Rising</li><li>Partial Falling </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You should use falling intonation at the end of a thought group or sentence to tell the listener that you are finished with that statement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Most people just make promises without paying too much attention to what they are saying.  </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Likewise, your  pitch will only partially fall at the end of a thought group to:<ul><li>give the listener's brain time to \u201cdigest\u201d the speech; and</li><li>tell the listener that you are not finished speaking.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Well ... I have to tell you ... </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you want to convince me of something ... to persuade me with a catchy phrase ... think again. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That's the honest truth ... I promise!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Well ... maybe I was much more gullible than you were. I believed everything!", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I mean ... remember when you were small? People made lots of promises.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to pay attention ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to focus on something or someone without distraction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People just make promises without paying too much attention to what they are saying.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about promises.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "gullible ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "easy to deceive; easily believes everything other people say", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe I was much more gullible than you were.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "zealously ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "done eagerly and with enthusiasm ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I ate my spinach zealously.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "robust ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "strong and healthy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was never what you'd call robust.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to intone ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say something slowly and seriously in a voice which does not rise or fall much", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: \"If you wear a sweater, you won't catch a cold,\" my mom lovingly intoned all winter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to come down with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to catch or show signs of an illness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I always come down with a cold in the winter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to ascertain ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to discover something, or to make sure of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It took me several years to ascertain that practice wasn't a magic formula.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "despite ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without being influenced or prevented by", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I always feel especially good despite promises which had nothing to do with reality", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "life's lessons ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "experiences from which useful knowledge or principles can be learned", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Despite life's lessons showing me that it's hard to work with others, I always feel especially good after playing basketball with my friends.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "That's the honest truth!", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to express deep sincerity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's the honest truth ...  I promise!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le12ob04aud10", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online or to the library and look up the lyrics to the song \"Promises, Promises\" written by Burt Bacharach.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read through them and say the lyrics aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now go find someone singing the song online or on CD at the library.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen without reading the lyrics the first time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go back to the lyrics and highlight words that you didn't hear or that were hard to hear.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen again with the lyrics sheet.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I find the lyrics and song to \"Promises, Promises\" written by Burt Bacharach.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read through the lyrics then listen to the song.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I note any words that were difficult to hear.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to the song again with the lyrics sheet.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le12ob04re2img03.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le12ob04re2img03.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Well ... I have to tell you ...  over the years, I've learned about people and promises! Most people just make promises without paying too much attention to what they are saying. I mean ... remember when you were small? People made lots of promises. I don't know about you, but I believed them all! Did you? Well ... maybe I was much more gullible than you were. I believed everything!"}, {"image": "engenn9le12ob04re2img02.jpg", "time": "31000", "id": 2, "text": "\"If you eat your spinach, you'll be strong,\" my grandmother used to say. I ate my spinach zealously ... I was never what you'd call robust. \"If you wear a sweater, you won't catch a cold,\" my mom lovingly intoned all winter. I always wear a sweater. Do you? I always come down with a cold as well!\n<br/><br/>My dad said, \"If you practice enough, you'll become a great basketball player.\" It took me several years to ascertain that practice wasn't a magic formula. I was never going to be a professional basketball player."}, {"image": "engenn9le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "73300", "id": 3, "text": "As an adult, I no longer believe in easy answers. What about you? If you want to convince me of something ... to persuade me with a catchy phrase ... think again.\n<br/><br/>Interestingly enough, despite life's lessons showing me that promises had nothing to do with reality,  I always feel especially good when I have spinach for dinner, put on a warm sweater, or go out into the yard to play a little basketball! That's the honest truth ... I promise!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le12ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le12ob04re2img03.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about friendship, relationships, feelings and reactions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can stress <span class=\"italic\">I</span> and <span class=\"italic\">you</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can use proper intonation in finished and unfinished ideas.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How often do you make promises?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you always keep your promises? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "Yo